            "review_id": "REV_3812617_p1_3",
            "reviewer_id": "User_p1_3",
            "review_title": "Review at Piero",
            "review_text": "Peter M\nDublin, Ireland22 contributions\n0\nMisleading, Rude and incompetent staff\nFeb 2013 • Friends\nWe had Pizzas and one had Borscht. Our waitress had poor English and little knowledge of the menu - that was fine - turns out she's a trainee. \nWe asked in advance what size the pizzas were and they told us large 25 cm and medium 20 cm. So we ordered large. The pizzas came and they were closer to 20 cm than 25 - we showed him and he admitted and apologies and said he would charge for small - the size of the pizza is not mentioned anywhere in the menu so I suspect that they normally get away with this as tourists do not ask the size. There were two large americans who ordered the small pizza and it was like a side plate - laughable.\n\nThen there was the borscht - it was tiny which was fine but there was not a sight of beef in the dish - the only thing that could be found was onion!\n\nSo when it came to the bill I asked that the borsch be taken off - I only took 2 spoonfuls. He said he couldn't do that, then he said he couldn't contact the manager. With some persuasion he gave me the managers number but insisted that I paid. I gave them the money and went to leave but he grabbed my arm. Upset as I was I left another wad of money behind.\n\nWhen I went back the staff where riffling through my money to get the 40K dong for the soup - really it was quite desperate. I decided not to pursue.\n\nBtw the pizza was nice but it's also nice in most of the other restaurants - I wouldn't chance it hear, and absentee manager/owner with incompetent staff and misleading menus is a recipe for disaster :-)\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 1, 2013",
